In the present case, according to prosecution story, three accused have committed offence of gang rape and victim remained consistent against the applicant in both her statements recorded under Sections 161 and 164 Cr.P.C.
Victim has disclosed the name of three accused including the applicant in her statement recorded under Section 161 Cr.P.C., but the name of Brajesh Kumar Yadav remained consistent in victim's statement recorded under Section 164 Cr.P.C., but other two co-accused were not identified.
Therefore, taking note the victim has not mentioned name of applicant in her statement recorded under Section 164 Cr.P.C., and similarly situated co-accused Sanjay Kumar @ Sanju has already been granted bail, therefore, the applicant who is in jail since 25.11.2022, as well as factor of overcrowding in jails, a case of bail is made out.
